\b SoundBridge Privacy Policy\b0\par
\par
\b Effective Date:\b0  June 2026\par
\b Developer:\b0  Prateek Kumar Singh / prateek271\par
\par
\b 1. Overview\b0\par
SoundBridge is a Windows desktop application for multi-output audio routing. This policy explains what data SoundBridge does and does not collect.\par
\par
The short version: SoundBridge does not collect, store, transmit, or share any personal data. It has no analytics, no telemetry, and no account system.\par
\par
\b 2. Data SoundBridge Does Not Collect\b0\par
SoundBridge does not collect or transmit personal information, audio content, usage analytics, crash reports, diagnostic data, location data, or data to third-party servers or services.\par
\par
The app routes audio between devices, but it never records, stores, or transmits audio content.\par
\par
\b 3. Data Stored Locally on Your Device\b0\par
SoundBridge stores configuration only on your local machine. This may include created routing templates, selected audio devices, volume levels, delay settings, and application preferences.\par
\par
Runtime data location:\par
%LocalAppData%\\SoundBridge\par
\par
Local files may include:\par
templates.json\par
templates.backup.json\par
logs\\app.log\par
corrupted\\*.bad.json\par
\par
This data never leaves your device. You can delete it manually by removing the local SoundBridge configuration folder.\par
\par
\b 4. Audio Data\b0\par
SoundBridge routes audio streams between Windows audio devices in real time. It does not record, store, analyse, or transmit audio content. Audio passes through application memory temporarily during routing and is immediately discarded. No audio data is written to disk.\par
\par
\b 5. Virtual Audio Device\b0\par
SoundBridge requires a virtual audio device for routing system audio. This MSI installer does not install the virtual audio device. The user is responsible for installing the required virtual audio device separately.\par
\par
\b 6. Network Access\b0\par
SoundBridge does not require internet access for normal operation. The app does not contact any server, cloud service, or remote endpoint during normal use.\par
\par
\b 7. Third-Party Components\b0\par
SoundBridge uses Microsoft .NET / WPF runtime components and a native Windows audio routing bridge. The virtual audio device is managed separately by the user.\par
\par
\b 8. Children's Privacy\b0\par
SoundBridge does not collect any data from any user, including minors.\par
\par
\b 9. Changes to This Policy\b0\par
If this policy is updated in a future version of SoundBridge, the new policy will be included in that release and the effective date will be updated.\par
\par
\b 10. Contact\b0\par
For questions about this privacy policy or how SoundBridge handles data, contact the developer: Prateek Kumar Singh / prateek271.\par
\par
SoundBridge collects nothing. Your audio, your devices, and your data stay on your machine.\par
\par
By continuing, you agree to install SoundBridge and allow it to store local app configuration for the current Windows user.\par
}
